# SHA-256 checksums of the files that download.sh fetches into ./binaries/.
# Format: `sha256sum` output ("<64 hex digits>  <file name>"), one line per file;
# download.sh checks each download against this list. The file is validated strictly
# (any malformed or duplicate line aborts download.sh): the hash is UNKNOWN or exactly
# 64 hex digits, the file name a bare name ([A-Za-z0-9._+-]+, optional leading `*`),
# LF or CRLF line ends.
#
# The hashes below were recorded from the release assets that download.sh fetches;
# to refresh them, download the files from a source you trust, check that they are
# the intended release files, then run in this directory:
#     (cd binaries && sha256sum *) | sort -k2 > /tmp/sums
# and replace the UNKNOWN lines below with the matching lines.
#
# While a hash is UNKNOWN, FIRMAE_VERIFY_DOWNLOADS decides: `strict` (default) rejects the
# file, `warn` keeps it and prints a warning. A known hash that
# does not match is always an error.
# Hashes recorded 2026-11-17 from https://github.com/pr0v3rbs/ (FirmAE_kernel-v2.6, FirmAE_kernel-v4.1, FirmAE releases, tag v1.0), two independent downloads matched; this pins the current assets, it does not prove their origin.
